# AutoBuild-H5000M-Openwrt feed configuration - mainline OpenWrt.
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: scripts/feeds strips comments with s/#.+$// and then skips
# blank lines. A lone "#" with nothing after it is therefore NOT a comment to
# that parser and dies with "Syntax error in feeds.conf.default". Every comment
# line here must have text after the hash.
# Upstream source is openwrt/openwrt (branch main, i.e. SNAPSHOT). The official
# OpenWrt feed repositories publish their development branch as master, which
# is what openwrt/openwrt's own feeds.conf.default references - keep that so
# the feeds stay in lockstep with the tree we build.
# Since OpenWrt 25.12 the package manager is apk, not opkg; CONFIG_PACKAGE_*
# symbols are unchanged and nothing here is ImmortalWrt-specific.

src-git packages https://github.com/openwrt/packages.git;master
src-git luci https://github.com/openwrt/luci.git;master
src-git routing https://github.com/openwrt/routing.git;master
src-git telephony https://github.com/openwrt/telephony.git;master
src-git video https://github.com/openwrt/video.git;master
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: every src-git line above names a BRANCH, so on its own this
# file produces a build that changes with the calendar. That is what actually
# broke QModem, and it took about twenty CI runs to see it. Three notes used to
# live here blaming the wwand feed, the video feed, and an upstream commit in
# scripts/package-metadata.pl; all three were tested and all three were wrong.
# The evidence: same tree, same upstream pin, 19 hours apart, and the only
# input that moved was feed content.
#     2026-09-29T12:40Z feeds -> 26 recursive deps, qmodem SURVIVED
#     2026-09-30T07:14Z feeds -> 176 recursive deps, qmodem DROPPED
# The delta is dated: openwrt/packages added `libdrm: depend on video-support`
# and `libevdev: depend on input-support` at 2026-09-29T14:50Z, 2h10m after
# the build that worked, and a tree pinned at bfb98589 has no such packages.
# So DO NOT try to fix a QModem drop by editing this list. Adjust
# FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE in configs/upstream.env instead - that is the knob that
# makes the feeds a fixed input, and pin_all_feeds() applies it.
# The video feed stays. Removing it changes the cycle count and changes nothing
# about qmodem, and the count does not decide the outcome anyway.
# wwand is NOT listed here.  It used to be an unconditional line, on the
# strength of three runs in which "wwand installed" correlated with "qmodem
# survived".  That was a correlation, and on 2026-10-07 it inverted:
#   ddimension/openwrt-repo 7889f403, 2026-10-06T15:39Z
#     "pcie_mhi: update to 1.6.0 and add NSS support, add rmnet-nss (#1)"
# added kmod-pcie_mhi_nss, which depends on kmod-mhi-pci-generic, which
# PACKAGE_qmodem selects - while PACKAGE_qmodem depends on kmod-pcie_mhi_nss.
# Kconfig reported the cycle and then dropped every symbol in it, so qmodem,
# luci-app-qmodem-next and luci-app-qmodem-generic all left the graph:
#   tmp/.config-package.in:34403:error: recursive dependency detected!
#     symbol PACKAGE_kmod-pcie_mhi_nss depends on PACKAGE_kmod-mhi-pci-generic
#     symbol PACKAGE_kmod-mhi-pci-generic is selected by PACKAGE_qmodem
#     symbol PACKAGE_qmodem depends on PACKAGE_kmod-pcie_mhi_nss
# Nothing in this feed is used on a QModem image, and one of its packages can
# take the whole modem stack out, so write_feeds_conf() appends it for
# ENABLE_WWAND=true only - which is what the WWAND_REPO_URL block in
# scripts/local-build.sh has said it did all along.


